## Why This Is Asked
 Tests ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant privacy enforcement and incident response workflow on GCP, including data lineage, per-tenant isolation, and automated remediation under real-time load.

## Key Concepts
 - Real-time data processing, per-tenant isolation, data masking, DLP, Vertex AI, Dataflow, Pub/Sub, Data Catalog lineage
 - Event-time vs processing-time semantics, idempotency, backpressure, rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record){
  const r = { ...record };
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-****';
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{1})(.*)(@)/, '$1***$2$3');
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the anomaly model under bursty traffic and schema drift?
- How would you handle false positives/negatives and post-incident cleanup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a candidate's ability to implement a straightforward streaming ingestion with validation, error handling, and rollback using familiar GCP primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub ingestion and Dataflow (Beam)
- JSON schema validation and field filtering
- BigQueryIO writes with insertId for idempotency and daily partitioning
- Dead-letter handling and Cloud Storage archival
- Lightweight testing and rollback planning

## Code Example
```javascript
function validate(record){
  if (typeof record.user_id !== 'string') return false;
  if (typeof record.event_time !== 'string') return false;
  if (typeof record.event_type !== 'string') return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle late-arriving data and schema evolution?
- What monitoring and alerting would you add for bad records and rollback validation?
